<title>JAPAN: Matsushita Elec up on share buy-back plan.</title>
<headline>Matsushita Elec up on share buy-back plan.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Matsushita Electric Works Ltd rose on the Tokyo Stock Exchange (TSE) on Tuesday morning, following the company's announcement that it would buy back its shares.</p>
<p>By 0038 GMT, the company's shares were up 23 yen at 1,010.</p>
<p>The company, a leading maker of building materials and lighting equipment, said on Monday that it plans to spend 50 billion yen to buy back 50 million of its shares from the market in the year following a shareholder's meeting planned for February 27.</p>
<p>Matsushita Electric Works is a group company of Japanese electronics giant Matsushita Electric Industrial Co Ltd.</p>
